# Normalize line endings explicitly, because the developer default on Windows is
# `core.autocrlf=true`, which would rewrite every checked-out file to CRLF.
#
# That default breaks this repository in two concrete ways, neither of them cosmetic:
#
#   1. tools/probe-distro.sh is PIPED TO BASH inside the distribution
#      (`Get-Content -Raw tools/probe-distro.sh | wsl.exe -- bash -s`). CRLF makes bash
#      read `;` and `$'\r'` as part of the command, so the script fails on line endings
#      rather than on logic. Observed directly while probing the distribution.
#   2. The helper is deployed into the distribution as loose files and its digest is
#      verified after upload. A checkout that silently changes bytes would change that
#      digest, so the same commit would verify on one machine and fail on another.
#
# Forcing LF keeps the working tree byte-identical across platforms.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit for the file types where the distinction actually matters.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.mjs   text eol=lf
*.cjs   text eol=lf
*.js    text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf

# PowerShell is CRLF-native on Windows; git should not touch it either way.
*.ps1   text eol=crlf

# Binary content must never be normalized.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.webp  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.svg   text eol=lf
*.node  binary

# The provisioned Node archive, if a cache is ever committed by mistake.
*.tar.xz binary
